# Git Conventions

- Never run git write operations (`git add`, `git commit`, `git push`) unless I explicitly instruct so in the current chat turn.
- Do not stage, commit, or push changes automatically.
- If a workflow normally requires a commit, show guidance only and annotate: `# Deviation: commit/push skipped per repo policy`.
- Conventional commits when I do ask: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `ci:`, `test:`.
- Never commit generated files, build artifacts, or `node_modules`.
